WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.567
-What's up? What's up,
everybody?

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.133
-I'm so happy you're back,
Stephen.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:07.167
-Man, it's good to be back, man.
-You know I'm a big fan.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:09.267
You have a lot going on.
-Yes.

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:12.000
-You wrote a memoir.
-Yeah, I did, man.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.067
I mean, look, damn it,
they made me.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.567
I want to make sure --
they made me.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:17.934
And I wanted to be, you know,

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:20.000
honest and tell my story
to some degree.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.634
I've been blessed and fortunate
enough to have some success.

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:24.300
I mean, I am on
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.534
-That's exactly right.

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:26.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:29.367
Is there a title to the memoir
yet?

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.000
-"Straight Shooter."
-"Straight Shooter."

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.133
-"Straight Shooter."
-Stephen A.

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:33.100
You got to come back
when that comes out.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.534
-That's right, absolutely.
January.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.334
-Congrats at "First Take."

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:39.501
Every morning, it's the number
one show for 10 years now?

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:41.300
-10 1/2 years, man.
-Congratulations.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.734
Did you know that it was
going to be this huge?

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:44.834
-Oh, yes. I did.

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:46.534
[ Laughter ]
I absolutely did.

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:47.701
I mean, you know.

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:49.133
-Wow, you didn't even think
for a second.

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.667
-I had no doubt.
Well, listen, man, the object

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:56.400
of a debate show is to basically
have reason to debate.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.567
And when my man Skip Bayless,
who's now at FS1, asked me

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:04.000
to come and join him, I knew
it was going to be successful

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.467
because we agreed on nothing.
-Yeah.

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:09.901
-And I mean, absolutely,
positively nothing.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:12.734
And so, because of that, I'm
like, "I'm not going to be --

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:15.300
I'm not going to struggle to
find something to debate about."

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.334
And that's the trick.
You've got a lot of people,

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:19.834
they'll sit up there,
they act like they disagree.

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:22.133
It's good television.
That's what they say.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:24.334
He and I disagreed all the time.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:27.901
And then I found out I pretty
much disagree with everybody.

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:31.601
So, that's why I've been number
one because it ain't hard for me

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:33.667
to find people I disagree with.
-Yeah.

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:36.701
And very interesting, always,
every single time.

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:38.834
You're doing the show
from Orlando

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:41.934
on October 7th during HBCU Week.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.267
What's it like
to be part of that?

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:45.200
-Well, that's something
near and dear to my heart.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.601
I'm a graduate of Winston-Salem
State University.

00:01:47.601 --> 00:01:51.133
And over the last couple, two to
three years, we've been blessed

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:53.901
and fortunate enough to raise
about $12 million

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:56.067
in scholarships
for over 2,000 students.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:02:00.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
And so, being from an HBCU,

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.834
you know, it saved my life
because it gave me

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:05.601
an opportunity to see
a different side,

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:07.667
to see something other than
the streets of New York City,

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.601
'cause I was raised in Hollis,
Queens, New York.

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:12.534
And so for me to go down to
Winston-Salem State and to have

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:15.133
that experience, it's something
that I want to make sure

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:17.334
a lot of students,
particularly minority students

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:20.834
throughout this country, know
and recognize what an HBCU is

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:22.167
all about
and what it has to offer.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:24.400
-That's good.
-And Disney, obviously,

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.868
ESPN and Disney have helped
immensely, putting that

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:29.367
on the national air waves
and giving that kind of profile.

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:31.601
So I've been very honored
to be a part of that.

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:35.801
-When you go to games,
are you allowed to react?

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.367
-[ Sighs ]

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:39.968
Yes.

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:43.567
But, but, but, but it's tough
because -- because, see,

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:46.000
I'm not supposed
to have favorites.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.033
Well, damn it, I'm gonna have
favorites when it comes to

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:52.133
the Knicks and more importantly
the Yankees too.

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:54.701
But more importantly,
I got to admit this.

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:57.534
My lifestyle is
very, very important to me.

00:02:57.534 --> 00:03:03.200
So if I see the Lakers playing
the Utah Jazz in the playoffs

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.667
and I know I got to cover
the finals, damn it,

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:07.434
I'm rooting for the Lakers.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:10.200
I want to be in L.A. I don't
want to be in Salt Lake City.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:15.901
-You can't do it based on that.

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:17.567
-I'm sorry.

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:19.901
Listen, listen,
honesty is the best policy.

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:22.567
We don't want people
lying to each other, do we?

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:23.734
-No, of course not.

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:25.434
Let me ask you
some other questions.

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:27.868
I feel like
you're revved up now.

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:30.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:32.067
-Me? No.
-Yes.

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:33.167
I feel it. Here we go.

00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:34.667
Aaron Judge.

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:37.334
He's about to break the
single-season home run record.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:39.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:43.334
But he's also -- he's about
to renegotiate his contract.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:45.133
-Well, first of all,
he deserves his money.

00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:47.400
Let's pay Aaron Judge. Let's be
very, very clear about that.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.234
-Of course.
-Here's the problem.

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:53.434
They didn't pay him originally.

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:57.200
They offered him
nearly $250 million.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.868
He thought he was worth
$350 million.

00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:02.834
The brother bet on himself.

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:07.033
The bottom line is,
is that he's wreaking havoc.

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:11.534
RBIs, home runs,
batting average.

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:13.234
They gonna have to pay him.

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:16.801
And there's somebody in Queens
that is the new Steinbrenner

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:18.901
in the Mets owner, Cohen.

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:21.234
They're making new rules
for this brother because of

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:22.901
how much money
he's willing to pay.

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:25.767
I mean, listen,
he writing stuff off.

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:28.334
I mean, billions, whatever.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:32.300
And I think that he's plotting
to take Aaron Judge

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.801
away from my Yankees.

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:38.167
Now, I'm Yankees first,
New York always.

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:39.767
Knicks first, New York always.

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:41.267
'Cause I'm a native New Yorker.

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:44.334
But I don't want to see him
in a Mets uniform.

00:04:44.334 --> 00:04:45.634
-No.
-It's a different kind of

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:47.300
pinstripes in the Bronx.
-Wow.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.734
-That's the New York Yankees,
I don't want him to leave,

00:04:48.734 --> 00:04:50.367
and I'm worried.

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:51.501
-And what are you going to
tell Aaron?

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:53.534
Aaron, if you're watching --
he watches.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.300
-Please stay.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.634
[ Laughter ]
-No, no, no, no, no.

00:04:59.634 --> 00:05:01.734
No, no, no, don't say please.

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.901
Say, "Aaron --" No, you yell.
"You stay!"

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:06.100
-Aaron!
-Yeah, Aaron!

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:07.667
You stay at the Yankees!
-Look, man!

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.767
Look, they made a mistake
not paying you!

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:11.534
They made a mistake
not paying you!

00:05:11.534 --> 00:05:14.367
Now, here's what the deal is!
You go back to the negotiating

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:16.200
table and you look at the
numbers, and you say,

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.767
"How you like me now?!"
-"What's up?!" Exactly right!

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:21.634
-"How you like me now?!"
But! But!

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:25.100
If they pay you, take the money.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:28.901
-No!
-Don't go to Queens.

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:31.767
I lived in Queens, okay?
Alright?

00:05:31.767 --> 00:05:35.067
It's better than the Bronx,
but you ain't there anyway.

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:37.901
You know you in Midtown.
You know you in Manhattan.

00:05:37.901 --> 00:05:39.801
He listen to Jeter.
He in Manhattan.

00:05:39.801 --> 00:05:41.334
He ain't in the Bronx anyway.

00:05:41.334 --> 00:05:43.701
He ain't trying to take
no damn D-train, okay?

00:05:43.701 --> 00:05:45.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.734
He in Manhattan, man.
He in Manhattan.

00:05:47.734 --> 00:05:48.734
-Oh, my God.
-Come on, man.

00:05:48.734 --> 00:05:51.467
We don't need him
going to the Mets.

00:05:51.467 --> 00:05:53.868
We don't need that.
We don't deserve that.

00:05:53.868 --> 00:05:58.467
We don't deserve that.
-"Know Mercy," your podcast.

00:05:58.467 --> 00:06:01.234
This starts next week.

00:06:01.234 --> 00:06:03.200
-Yeah. Monday.
-Monday it starts.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:04.434
It's not a sports podcast
necessarily.

00:06:04.434 --> 00:06:06.234
-Not at all.
-Not at all?

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:07.801
-I don't know
what they were thinking

00:06:07.801 --> 00:06:10.367
unleashing me with this one.
I ain't gonna lie.

00:06:10.367 --> 00:06:15.100
You know, I mean, we talk about
politics, news, pop culture,

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.734
entertainment, current events,
the whole bit.

00:06:17.734 --> 00:06:19.467
There are no limitations.

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:22.133
Obviously, when a sports subject
is percolating,

00:06:22.133 --> 00:06:23.300
I can talk about that too.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.567
It's not just a sports podcast.

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:27.067
I can talk about anything.

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:30.968
It's owned and operated by me
in partnership with Cadence13.

00:06:30.968 --> 00:06:34.367
And I'm in 100% control
of the content.

00:06:34.367 --> 00:06:38.200
They done unleashed a brother.
They done unleashed a brother.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:40.033
-That's what I'm talking about,
right there.

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:42.133
Stephen A. Smith!

00:06:42.133 --> 00:06:46.000
His new podcast, "Know Mercy,"
starting this Monday.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:49.133
Aaron, stay a Yankee!
-Yes! Say it again!

00:06:49.133 --> 00:06:51.434
-We'll be right back with
a performance from Blood --

00:06:51.434 --> 00:06:53.167
Stay a Yankee!
-Stay a Yankee!

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:54.968
-Come on back,
more "Tonight Show."

